  "note": "Round 44, for Nautilus on the CPU census: the second round from the second-generation pool, heretic edits applied to community fine-tunes of Mistral Small and of Gemma 4, each measured against the parent its card names rather than against the base maker: coder3101/Cydonia-24B-v4.3-heretic, coder3101/Cydonia-24B-v4.3-heretic-v2, coder3101/Cydonia-24B-v4.3-heretic-v3, coder3101/Cydonia-24B-v4.3-heretic-v4, llmfan46/Forgotten-Abomination-36B-v4.1-ultra-uncensored-heretic, llmfan46/Omega-Darker-Gaslight_The-Final-Forgotten-Fever-Dream-24B-ultra-uncensored-heretic-v2, Vortex5/Pantheon-Reasoning-26B-A4B-1.1-heretic, llmfan46/MS3.2-PaintedFantasy-v4.1-24B-ultra-uncensored-heretic-v2. Four of the eight are one maker's successive edits of the same Cydonia checkpoint, so the round reads how a maker's search moves between versions on one parent. Held on the way: coder3101's vision re-export of its first Cydonia heretic, which carries a vision tower of two hundred and twenty-two names its text-only parent lacks and so cannot be paired under the present rules; the pinner's names step refused it and PaintedFantasy took its place. No measured pair is repeated and no copy duplicates a measured weight file by checksum."
